@startuml
title Coordinated runtime shutdown
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam componentBorderColor #475569
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam packageBorderColor #64748B
hide empty description
state Running
state Draining
state Stopped
[*] --> Running : initialize runtime
Running --> Draining : observe shutdown latch\nImmediate or Drain { timeout }
Draining : close ordinary admission and intake
Draining : reject queued commands; quiesce drivers
Draining : invoke on_shutdown once with separate effect allowance
Draining : final output still obeys hard byte/message quotas
Draining --> Draining : shorten drain deadline\nor escalate to immediate
Draining --> Stopped : output empty, deadline reached\nor immediate requested
Running --> Stopped : fatal failure or unwind cleanup
Draining --> Stopped : fatal failure or unwind cleanup
Stopped --> [*]
note right of Stopped
Close resources and disable control admission.
Report unresolved write offsets and registrations.
On unwind, clean up and resume the original panic.
Drop is abortive and does not invoke callbacks.
end note
note left of Draining
Monotonic deadline bounds controlled waiting.
It cannot preempt application callbacks.
The acceptance example separately uses a worker
shutdown guard and a process watchdog.
end note
@enduml
